Blackdrift: install as org.sonicon.browser instead of org.mozilla.focus.

Why: Blackdrift must not share an application ID with Mozilla Firefox Focus, so it
can be installed side by side with the real app and never receives its updates,
data, or Play Store identity. Only the applicationId changes; the Kotlin
namespace and source package stay org.mozilla.focus to keep this patch small.
The flavor-level applicationId replaces defaultConfig "org.mozilla" + ".focus";
build-type suffixes still apply, so focusDebug installs as
org.sonicon.browser.debug and focusRelease as org.sonicon.browser. Klar is untouched.

The static launcher shortcuts hardcode their targetPackage per variant, so they
must follow the new ID or long-press shortcuts would launch (or fail to find)
the real Focus app.

Cut against: mozilla-firefox/firefox@6181e6b5f28a8fbae1d5c3ef6f6626b5a2180213 (Firefox 159.0.1).

diff --git a/app/build.gradle b/app/build.gradle
index 902c60c..3be908f 100644
--- a/app/build.gradle
+++ b/app/build.gradle
@@ -132,7 +132,7 @@ android {
         focus {
             dimension "product"
 
-            applicationIdSuffix ".focus"
+            applicationId "org.sonicon.browser"
 
             // This is used when the user selects text in other third-party apps. See https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/focus-android/issues/6478
             manifestPlaceholders = [textSelectionSearchAction: "@string/text_selection_search_action_focus"]
diff --git a/app/src/focusBeta/res/xml-v25/shortcuts.xml b/app/src/focusBeta/res/xml-v25/shortcuts.xml
index daaece8..5b29b3a 100644
--- a/app/src/focusBeta/res/xml-v25/shortcuts.xml
+++ b/app/src/focusBeta/res/xml-v25/shortcuts.xml
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@
         android:shortcutLongLabel="@string/shortcut_erase_long_label">
         <intent
             android:action="erase"
-            android:targetPackage="org.mozilla.focus.beta"
+            android:targetPackage="org.sonicon.browser.beta"
             android:targetClass="org.mozilla.focus.activity.EraseShortcutActivity">
                 <extra android:name="shortcut" android:value="true" />
         </intent>
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
       android:shortcutShortLabel="@string/shortcut_erase_and_open_short_label">
     <intent
         android:action="erase"
-        android:targetPackage="org.mozilla.focus.beta"
+        android:targetPackage="org.sonicon.browser.beta"
         android:targetClass="org.mozilla.focus.activity.EraseAndOpenShortcutActivity">
       <extra android:name="shortcut" android:value="true" />
     </intent>
